  "query_preview": "(Monday through Thursday)...\nOnshore flow will begin to strengthen on Monday and begin to\nspread cooling inland with Monday high temperatures a few to\naround 5 degrees above average. A low pressure system moving into\nCalifornia some time around late Tuesday and Wednesday will bring\ncooler and breezy conditions along with a slight chance of \nshowers. High temperatures for next Wednesday will fall to around \naverage near the coast to 5 to locally 10 degrees below average \nfor the mountains. High temperatures for next Wednesday will \nrange from the mid to upper 60s near the cast to the lower to mid \n70s for the Inland Empire with the lower deserts in the lower to \nmid 80s.",
